					<![CDATA[
						 <p>&quot;The tragedy of the Human for is one of wasted opportunities. Consider the teeth: a perfect vice/cutting tool, dependent on the stringy fibers of muscle and the constantly-degrading structures of human bone to function. With the implementation of certain Standardized reinforcement structures and a large-scale material replacement, the teeth and jaws can be made to serve a purpose as admirable as the Hand.&quot;</p> <p>-Sister Curette, <em>The Tyranny of the Organic</em></p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
